+    The card's worst measured SD write stall in the logger's own pattern, which core EMB-6 sizes the RAM log buffer against
+    ("at least the log rate x the card's worst measured SD write stall"). Measured on the FC3v2 Rev-C board with its 64 GB FAT32
+    card, bench log image (MARV_FC3V2_LOG_BENCH: 1 GiB preallocated file, 16 KiB direct multi-sector writes, no FAT or directory
+    write while logging; tests/regression/quad/L10/results/log_bench/README.md). Rule: the stall is the most cells the ring held at
+    the end of any data write (log_bench backlog_post_write_max) x 16 B, divided by the fast stream's 314011.5 B/s, rounded up to
+    the millisecond, taken as the maximum over the instrumented runs: 30-minute soak 5358 cells = 0.273 s; 10-minute EMB-3
+    capture 9618 cells = 153888 B = 0.4901 s; so 0.491 s. The two runs differ by a factor 1.8, so the figure is a lower bound on
+    the true worst case: it rests on two runs of one card. The longest single write was 161.6 to 163.3 ms in all three runs
+    (about 17 writes per 30 minutes in the 131-164 ms bucket); the ring's fill beyond that is the logger's own work around it.
+    0 ring drops while logging, 0 write failures, the whole 568 MB soak file decoded clean. A card of another make or wear may
+    stall longer, and the flight image's own background work (link service, telemetry) is not in the measurement; the flight image
+    repeats it (unit U4). Replaces the earlier PLACEHOLDER 0.809 s (unit 13's hal_config_pending_write, a different pattern).
+    Used by test code and by the logger's pre-roll derivation (invariant L-5; fw/log budget.hpp).
   used_by: [onboard SD flight logger (fw/log) ring sizing L-5 and derived pre-roll, core EMB-6]
